\begin_layout Standard
Since 
\begin_inset Formula $u_{i}(x_{i}),i=1,2$
\end_inset

 are differentiable and quasi-concave, then a necessary and sufficient condition
 for the feasible interior points to be Parteo optimal (PO) is that 
\begin_inset Formula $MRS_{x_{1,}y_{1}}=MRS_{x_{2},y_{2}}$
\end_inset

.
 Note, 
\begin_inset Formula $MRS_{1}=y_{1}$
\end_inset

 and 
\begin_inset Formula $MRS_{2}=\frac{y_{2}}{2}$
\end_inset

.
 Setting these two equations equal to one another we have
\begin_inset Formula 
\begin{eqnarray*}
y_{1} & = & \frac{y_{2}}{2}\\
2y_{1} & = & (4-y_{1})\\
y_{1} & = & \frac{4}{3}
\end{eqnarray*}

\end_inset

Thus, the set of Pareto optimal allocations is given by:
\begin_inset Formula 
\[
PO=\left\{ (a_{1},a_{2})\in X_{1}\times X_{2}:a_{1}+a_{2}=(6,4)\ \wedge\ y_{1}=\frac{4}{3}\right\} 
\]

\end_inset


