\begin_layout Standard
An allocation 
\begin_inset Formula $x$
\end_inset

 is said to be fair if it is both Pareto optimal and equitable.
 We have already found the set of PO allocations, so let us now characterize
 the set of IR allocations.
 An allocation 
\begin_inset Formula $x$
\end_inset

 is equitable if 
\begin_inset Formula $\forall\ i\in N,\forall\ k\in N:x_{i}\succsim_{i}x_{k}$
\end_inset

.
 So, equitable allocations must satisfy
\begin_inset Formula 
\begin{eqnarray*}
e^{x_{1}}y_{1} & \geq & e^{x_{2}}y_{2}\\
e^{x_{1}}\frac{4}{3} & \geq & e^{(6-x_{1})}\frac{8}{3}\\
e^{2x_{1}} & \geq & 2e^{6}\\
2x_{1} & \geq & 6+\ln2\\
x_{1} & \geq & \frac{6+\ln2}{2}
\end{eqnarray*}

\end_inset

and
\begin_inset Formula 
\begin{eqnarray*}
e^{x_{2}}y_{2}^{2} & \geq & e^{x_{1}}y_{1}^{2}\\
e^{(6-x_{1})}\frac{64}{9} & \geq & e^{x_{1}}\frac{16}{9}\\
4e^{6} & \geq & e^{2x_{1}}\\
\frac{6+\ln4}{2} & \geq & x_{1}
\end{eqnarray*}

\end_inset

Thus, the set of fair allocations is given by
\begin_inset Formula 
\[
F=\left\{ (a_{1},a_{2})\in X_{1}\times X_{2}:a_{1}+a_{2}=(6,4),y_{1}=\frac{4}{3},3+\frac{1}{2}\ln2\leq x_{1}\leq3+\ln2\right\} 
